1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:09,862
A trainer has to turn a procedure into a graded course the LMS can track, and know the package works before anyone uploads it.

2
00:00:09,862 --> 00:00:17,414
Scrimshaw builds the course, drafts the first quiz through Fairlead, and publishes a SCORM package.

3
00:00:17,414 --> 00:00:22,831
The procedure and the learner are synthetic, and the LMS is a stand-in.

4
00:00:23,081 --> 00:00:24,912
It all runs on this one computer.

5
00:00:24,912 --> 00:00:32,112
Launch dot bat starts a small PowerShell server on loopback, and the editor and player run in your browser.

6
00:00:32,812 --> 00:00:38,630
Courses autosave in browser storage, with a dot scrim file for backup.

7
00:00:39,130 --> 00:00:47,763
In: slides you build, PowerPoint, and media files from Capstan, SnapShackle and TalkForge.

8
00:00:48,223 --> 00:00:53,039
Out: SCORM, xAPI, cmi5, a web page, a storyboard and a Word handout.

9
00:00:53,739 --> 00:00:54,646
AI is optional.

10
00:00:54,646 --> 00:01:03,350
The model key sits in Lazarette, shared to Fairlead, and Scrimshaw asks Fairlead for a draft with its own client key.

11
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:06,599
There is also a command line and a loopback API.

12
00:01:06,599 --> 00:01:11,543
Planned: handing the key over from Lazarette directly.

13
00:01:12,107 --> 00:01:20,673
Guardrails: loopback only, drafts are opt-in and reviewed by you, publishing is checked, and the server stops when the tab closes.

14
00:01:20,923 --> 00:01:27,717
The model key lives in Lazarette, the encrypted vault, and is shared once with Fairlead.

15
00:01:27,717 --> 00:01:33,303
This footage is from the Halyard demo: the same key, set up once for every tool.

16
00:01:34,003 --> 00:01:39,589
Launch dot bat starts Scrimshaw on port eighty-seven seventy-five, its place in the Fleet port registry.

17
00:01:40,289 --> 00:01:44,636
Fairlead has a client named Scrimshaw, so its calls can be told apart in the log.

18
00:01:45,336 --> 00:01:50,614
And the page address is allowed as a browser origin, because the page calls Fairlead directly.

19
00:01:51,114 --> 00:01:52,272
Start a new course and name it.

20
00:01:52,632 --> 00:01:54,045
The passing score is eighty percent.

21
00:01:54,745 --> 00:01:57,436
Drafting is off until you turn it on.

22
00:01:57,436 --> 00:02:03,478
This PC has no local model, so I allow a cloud engine, and only a made-up procedure goes through.

23
00:02:03,478 --> 00:02:06,761
The client key stays in memory for this session.

24
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:09,448
Draft asks the model through Fairlead.

25
00:02:10,332 --> 00:02:12,172
This is the live wait, sped up.

26
00:02:12,872 --> 00:02:17,397
Three questions come back, but nothing is in the course until I add them.

27
00:02:17,397 --> 00:02:21,652
Then I review each question and the answer it marks correct.

28
00:02:21,652 --> 00:02:24,699
The model can be wrong, so the author decides.

29
00:02:25,399 --> 00:02:31,704
Fairlead keeps its own log: client Scrimshaw, model GPT-5 mini, status two hundred.

30
00:02:31,954 --> 00:02:36,510
Publish offers SCORM, xAPI, a web page or the project file.

31
00:02:36,510 --> 00:02:39,067
I take SCORM one point two.

32
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:41,888
Inside are the manifest and the player, one file.

33
00:02:42,429 --> 00:02:45,863
The eighty percent pass mark travels in the manifest.

34
00:02:46,373 --> 00:02:50,027
Now a learner takes it in a stand-in LMS I wrote for this video.

35
00:02:50,027 --> 00:02:58,577
It is not a real LMS, but it speaks the SCORM calls, and every call the package makes is logged on the right.

36
00:02:58,577 --> 00:03:01,732
First attempt: one answer wrong on purpose.

37
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:06,000
Sixty-seven percent, under the pass mark, so the LMS is told failed.

38
00:03:06,654 --> 00:03:11,939
Retry with every answer right: a hundred percent, and the status is passed.

39
00:03:12,458 --> 00:03:14,637
That record is the evidence.

40
00:03:14,637 --> 00:03:19,826
A real LMS is the final check: this proves the package, not any one vendor.

41
00:03:20,131 --> 00:03:28,564
The model drafted, a person checked every answer, and the result was recorded by the LMS, here a stand-in.

42
00:03:28,564 --> 00:03:33,497
Not shown: PowerPoint import, xAPI, cmi5 and the command line.

43
00:03:33,497 --> 00:03:36,876
No minutes-saved number is claimed.
